"use strict";(Array.isArray(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs)?self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs:self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=[]).push([[3037],{81858(e,t,n){n.r(t),n.d(t,{comp:()=>a,data:()=>i});var r=n(20641);const o={},a=(0,n(66262).A)(o,[["render",function(e,t){return(0,r.uX)(),(0,r.CE)("div",null,t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,r.Fv)('<h1 id="ai-usage-limits-quotas" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#ai-usage-limits-quotas"><span>AI Usage Limits &amp; Quotas</span></a></h1><p>To keep marketplace operations predictable and protect store owners from unexpected third-party API bills, <strong>Magic AI</strong> includes built-in usage governance.</p><p>Marketplace administrators configure a single, centralized global quota setting that governs how often each vendor can generate AI content across the store.</p><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Budget Protection &amp; Equal Access</p><p>Configuring usage limits ensures every vendor has predictable access to AI tools to draft their product listings, while preventing runaway costs or API exhaustion.</p></div><hr><h2 id="how-generations-are-counted" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-generations-are-counted"><span>How Generations Are Counted</span></a></h2><p>Magic AI tracks vendor usage using clear, transparent rules:</p><ul><li><strong>Full Product Generation:</strong> Running a multi-field generation request (from the modal assistant or the &quot;Create Product with AI&quot; launcher) consumes <strong>1 generation</strong>.</li><li><strong>Single-Field Generation / Refinement:</strong> Clicking an inline field Magic AI button or clicking &quot;Regenerate this field&quot; inside the review step consumes <strong>1 generation</strong>.</li><li><strong>Image Enhancement:</strong> Enhancing a product thumbnail image consumes <strong>1 generation</strong>.</li><li><strong>Non-Destructive Review:</strong> Previewing generated text, unchecking fields, or canceling a generation modal <strong>does not consume additional generations</strong>. Generations are only deducted when the AI engine produces content.</li><li><strong>Failed or Dropped Requests:</strong> If an external AI provider encounters a network error, downtime, or temporary timeout, the request is <strong>not counted</strong> against the vendor&#39;s balance.</li><li><strong>Concurrent Request Protection:</strong> A vendor can only run one active generation at a time to prevent duplicate simultaneous API calls.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="global-limit-configuration-for-all-vendors" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#global-limit-configuration-for-all-vendors"><span>Global Limit Configuration for All Vendors</span></a></h2><p>Marketplace administrators configure usage quotas centrally under <strong>WordPress Admin &gt;&gt; Marketplace &gt;&gt; Magic AI &gt;&gt; Marketplace Features &gt;&gt; Limits</strong>:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Setting Field</th><th>Control Type</th><th>Description &amp; Behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Per Seller Limit</strong></td><td>Number / Text Input</td><td>Maximum generations allowed per vendor within the chosen timeframe. Leave blank for <strong>unlimited</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Limit Period</strong></td><td>Dropdown Selector</td><td>Quota reset cycle: <strong>Monthly</strong> (default), <strong>Weekly</strong>, <strong>Daily</strong>, or <strong>Lifetime</strong>.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="_1-per-seller-limit" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-per-seller-limit"><span>1. Per Seller Limit</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Global Setting, Individual Quota:</strong> This is a <strong>single global setting</strong> configured by the store administrator that applies uniformly to <strong>every vendor</strong> across the entire marketplace.</li><li><strong>Independent Allowances:</strong> If the limit is set to <code>25</code>, <strong>each vendor receives their own independent allowance of 25 generations</strong> for the selected cycle. It is <em>not</em> a shared collective pool where one vendor&#39;s usage depletes another&#39;s allowance.</li><li><strong>Unlimited Mode:</strong> Leaving this field blank or empty grants <strong>unlimited generations</strong> to all vendors.</li></ul><h3 id="_2-limit-period" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-limit-period"><span>2. Limit Period</span></a></h3><p>Defines the time window over which each seller&#39;s generations are counted before resetting:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Reset Period</th><th>Reset Schedule</th><th>Recommended Use Case</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Monthly (Default)</strong></td><td>Resets on the 1st of each calendar month at 00:00 UTC</td><td>Standard marketplace operations with predictable monthly billing cycles.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Weekly</strong></td><td>Resets every Monday at 00:00 UTC</td><td>Fast-moving marketplaces with high catalog turnover.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Daily</strong></td><td>Resets every night at midnight (00:00 UTC)</td><td>High-volume stores encouraging regular daily product listing workflows.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Lifetime</strong></td><td>Permanent hard cap that never resets automatically</td><td>Trial accounts or initial vendor onboarding programs.</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h2 id="centralized-architecture-vendor-quota-tracking" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#centralized-architecture-vendor-quota-tracking"><span>Centralized Architecture &amp; Vendor Quota Tracking</span></a></h2><p>Magic AI uses a streamlined, centralized approach so marketplace owners don&#39;t have to configure or maintain dozens of individual vendor settings:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Central Marketplace Setting</th><th>How It Applies to Individual Vendors</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Admin sets Global Quota in Marketplace Features</strong><br><em>(Example: 25 generations per month)</em></td><td><strong>Every active vendor receives their own independent 25 generations:</strong><br>• <strong>Vendor A:</strong> 25 generations / month (12 used, 13 remaining)<br>• <strong>Vendor B:</strong> 25 generations / month (0 used, 25 remaining)<br>• <strong>Vendor C:</strong> 25 generations / month (25 used, quota reached)</td></tr></tbody></table><ol><li><strong>One Central Control:</strong> Admins configure the limit once in the <strong>Marketplace Features</strong> tab. There is no need to manually edit individual vendor profiles or manage separate user roles.</li><li><strong>Individual Background Balances:</strong> In the background, Magic AI tracks each vendor&#39;s consumption independently in their account record, tied to the active reset cycle (monthly, weekly, daily, or lifetime).</li><li><strong>Automatic Period Rollover:</strong> When a new period starts (e.g., the 1st of the next month), the vendor&#39;s period counter rolls over automatically with zero manual admin intervention.</li><li><strong>Hands-Off Maintenance:</strong> Store administrators configure the quota once globally. The marketplace automatically manages individual vendor balances and enforces allowances with zero daily administration.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="live-quota-tracking-for-vendors" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#live-quota-tracking-for-vendors"><span>Live Quota Tracking for Vendors</span></a></h2><p>Vendors receive full transparency into their current usage directly inside the Magic AI generation interfaces (both the &quot;Generate content&quot; modal and the &quot;Create Product with AI&quot; wizard):</p><table><thead><tr><th>In-Modal Meter Component</th><th>Appearance &amp; Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Live Usage Text</strong></td><td>Displays current generation count: <code>12 / 25 generations used</code> (or <code>12 generations used</code> when unlimited).</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Progress Indicator Bar</strong></td><td>Visual colored bar showing percentage of quota consumed within the active period.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Generation Safeguard</strong></td><td>When the limit is reached, the <strong>Generate</strong> button is disabled and displays an explanatory tooltip notice.</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="in-modal-meter-features" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#in-modal-meter-features"><span>In-Modal Meter Features</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Active Generation Counter:</strong> Shows real-time usage (e.g., <code>12 / 25 generations used</code>). If the marketplace is configured for unlimited generations, it shows <code>12 generations used</code>.</li><li><strong>Dynamic Progress Bar:</strong> Visual progress indicator displaying consumption percentage.</li><li><strong>Limit Reached Safeguard:</strong> When a vendor reaches their maximum generation allowance: <ul><li>The <strong>Generate</strong> button is automatically disabled.</li><li>A descriptive tooltip informs the seller: <em>&quot;You have reached your generation limit for this period&quot;</em>.</li><li>Vendors can still manually edit, create, and publish products without any interruption.</li><li>The quota automatically renews once the active period expires.</li></ul></li></ul>',28)]))}]]),i=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/usage-limits.html","title":"AI Usage Limits & Quotas","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"How Generations Are Counted","slug":"how-generations-are-counted","link":"#how-generations-are-counted","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Global Limit Configuration for All Vendors","slug":"global-limit-configuration-for-all-vendors","link":"#global-limit-configuration-for-all-vendors","children":[{"level":3,"title":"1. Per Seller Limit","slug":"_1-per-seller-limit","link":"#_1-per-seller-limit","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"2. Limit Period","slug":"_2-limit-period","link":"#_2-limit-period","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Centralized Architecture & Vendor Quota Tracking","slug":"centralized-architecture-vendor-quota-tracking","link":"#centralized-architecture-vendor-quota-tracking","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Live Quota Tracking for Vendors","slug":"live-quota-tracking-for-vendors","link":"#live-quota-tracking-for-vendors","children":[{"level":3,"title":"In-Modal Meter Features","slug":"in-modal-meter-features","link":"#in-modal-meter-features","children":[]}]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/usage-limits.md"}')}}]);